{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers satisfy the equation \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18dfc63240b01569b535ba05a0d53841ad6cfe8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot b + 63 = 20\\cdot \\text{lcm}(a, b) + 12\\cdot\\text{gcd}(a,b),\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dff0965f3110a4b6dc0b69e8aa5cabecaab653c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest common divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc7ea17e24bf9f5800940d8858ee3af0ecf4582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{lcm}(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> denotes their least common multiple?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce516a86a77759c0696a641f14335cc08da1be22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ 0} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\text{ 2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\text{ 4} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\text{ 6} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\text{ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"345\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428f1394d22004ad9f2270f64eec9706bce991b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\text{lcm}(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e66706a694e1ee0b8ace35b68bc9c3465aaef721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\text{gcd}(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/41085df9aff987ca8d8ddfe876fd7a46b8f149bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot b = \\text{lcm}(a, b)\\cdot \\text{gcd}(a, b) = x\\cdot y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"257\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, the equation becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fabf3251ab45c9a46352eae222bfb87de8a20b11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\cdot y + 63 = 20x + 12y\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82bc19a6185adaf76a5daddc460ab02f14038347.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\cdot y - 20x - 12y + 63 = 0\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simon%27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick\" title=\"Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick\">Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick</a>, we rewrite this equation as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f15f9030f3a91e97f5177a080c2c67d39bb18996.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x - 12)(y - 20) - 240 + 63 = 0\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa4468ebc4559a0d0b039d0184912c1b30586cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x - 12)(y - 20) = 177\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0ca2a9ea48473aa074ead204a709d33561cc08f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$177 = 3\\cdot 59$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cff74c9835800e1bdd71946257c780cf4df57af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt;= y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/3063ff89e3f5da0bcda72985181ff609623e0ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x  - 12 = 59$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d162d2a824d4fc37562fda575edd114acdfb1836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - 20 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/310d23ba8472cdfbe1d1a964112655f27e65ec31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 12 = 177$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"102\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5da9c4d81bb35045944f9f044f6df3cf279fd28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - 20 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />. This gives us the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be416b454efce5d2c8ae197236cd20b061d0997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(71, 23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471767c687786e3621c3b846c4d437103cf083a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(189, 21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee0bac9892398b786946d4829d082e3c3c70041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{GCD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> must be a divisor of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c90c80a99ee3736d931647e05b88d1f3ec6321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{LCM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" />, the first pair does not work. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. We must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b993de9e1eb92a149caf15d40137901728a59a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 21 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02ee40a14f381cd4b402bfc2e0bc77e3ba6667ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, and we could then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710e3e4f18d7c0270ab719a00adc61fa12363b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cdb0dfdd4fb60dccd2ff46af2eac89a17db6fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} ~2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" /> solutions.\n(awesomeag)\n</p><p>Edited by IronicNinja, Firebolt360, and mprincess0229~\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=494\">https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=494</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JWGHYUeOx-k\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JWGHYUeOx-k</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsecti